18:- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and is passed `totalUsage` — the sum of the usage every provider call in the turn reported, not the last round alone ([validated by: sums the usage of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L598)).
19:- A rejection that is already an `Error` reaches `onError` as that same instance, while a string or object thrown inside the turn is wrapped in an `Error` with a readable `message`, keeping the thrown value as the wrapper's `cause` ([validated by: wraps a thrown string in an Error whose cause is that string](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L311)).
20:- A rejection with `undefined` is wrapped the same way, its `cause` is `undefined`, and the caller still receives `undefined` itself ([validated by: wraps an undefined rejection for onError while the caller still receives undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L330)).
21:- A thrown string reaches `onError` as an `Error` whose `message` is that string, and then `afterSession` runs while the original string still propagates to the caller ([validated by: calls onError with an Error carrying the thrown string and runs afterSession while rethrowing](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L53)).
